        <body>
            <div xml:id="d491">

                <pb facs="0541" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg491"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tyler to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 118.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my No. 115 of July 25 I had the honor to
                    transmit a copy and translation of a letter which I had addressed to the
                    Mushir-ul-Mulk regarding the proposal of Mr. Hawkes, a missionary in Hamadan, to
                    open a school in Kermanshah for the instruction of Jewish and Christian children
                    in that city. I now beg to forward his excellency’s reply, which, it will be
                    observed, is still unfavorable.</p>
                <p>Whether the troubles in Hamadan have had anything to do with this refusal I do
                    not know, but at any rate the Government seem to have made up their minds on the
                    subject, and I think that any further application would be useless at the
                    present.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Tyler</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul-General in
                    charge.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d491-a1.xml" xpointer="d491-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
